SUMMARY:10-Minute Talk: The Legend of Sleepy Hollow
LOCATION:Museum of the American Revolution\, 101 S 3rd St\, Philadelphia\, 
 PA 19106
DESCRIPTION:Head to the Museum of the American Revolution for a 10-minute\,
  in-gallery talk about the legend of Sleepy Hollow.\n\nIt is believed that
  The Legend of Sleepy Hallow\, Washington Irving’s gothic tale about the
  ghostly Headless Horseman\, was based on a Hessian soldier who was decapi
 tated by cannonball fire.\n\nMeet in the Trenton and Princeton gallery dai
 ly at 12:30 p.m. (except Oct. 10-12) for this talk.\n\nEvent website: http
 s://www.amrevmuseum.org/events/10-minute-talk-the-legend-of-sleepy-hollow\
 n\nListing: https://phillyfamily.com/event/10-minute-talk-the-legend-of-sl
 eepy-hollow/2027-10-23/
URL:https://www.amrevmuseum.org/events/10-minute-talk-the-legend-of-sleepy-
 hollow
CATEGORIES:Community Event,For The Whole Family
END:VEVENT
